---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Disclaimer from "../components/Disclaimer.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/paths";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Style guide"
  description="Sporty Media house style: education first, no locks, no guaranteed winners, Ontario disclaimers."
>
  <article class="wrap article-wrap">
    <header class="post-hero">
      <p class="kicker">House style</p>
      <h1>Education first. No locks.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        These rules keep Sporty Media from sliding into tipster copy. Use them on every post,
        including board notes.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Positioning</h2>
      <p>
        We write about <strong>markets</strong>: prices, fees, information, and uncertainty. We do
        not write as if the reader should place a bet tonight. A useful piece leaves someone better
        at reading a board. It does not leave them with a ticket.
      </p>

      <h2>Banned language</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Lock, smash, hammer, can’t lose, guaranteed, easy money.</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Pick, play of the day, best bet</strong> used as a recommendation.</li>
        <li>Promises about units, seasons, or “beating the books” as a service.</li>
        <li>Fake certainty: “sharps are all over this” without a source or a caveat.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Preferred language</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Number, price, close, juice, hold, overround, CLV, steam, grind, board note.</li>
        <li>“The market moved X because Y is reported” — not “bet the move.”</li>
        <li>“This would have been plus / minus CLV if you had the open” — hypothetical, labeled.</li>
        <li>Unknowns listed in public, the same way a good note lists them in private.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Board notes</h2>
      <p>
        A board note explains a <em>shift</em>, not a side. Use the
        <a href={withBase("/posts/board-notes-mlb-nfl-template/")}>MLB / NFL template</a>: open →
        current → close (if available), who followed, news vs money, and what you still do not know.
        Never end a note with a wager.
      </p>

      <h2>Examples</h2>
      <p>Examples should be round numbers and clearly hypothetical unless they are historical.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Good: “You bet −110; the close is −120. That ticket beat the close.”</li>
        <li>Bad: “Take the under tonight, the close is going to be a gift.”</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        Every page carries the Ontario disclaimer: risk of loss, 19+, responsible play. Do not hide
        it in the footer only. Put a copy near the article as well.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <Disclaimer />
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
